        "3.4 Why the three tensions matter in communication\nA message can be relevant because it:\n- Names a problem someone wants to avoid.\n- Recognises an identity or group they care about.\n- Shows a future they want to move toward.\nA strong message does not need to activate all three. It should connect to the audience's actual situation.",
