        "4.1 The desire to reduce risk\nPeople pay attention to problems that threaten something they value. The threat might be large or small, immediate or distant.",
        "Examples include:\n- Losing money through a poor decision.\n- Wasting months on an ineffective approach.\n- Missing a relevant opportunity.\n- Feeling unprepared for a change in their industry.\n- Spending too much time on a repetitive task.\n- Making a mistake that damages trust.\nA message becomes relevant when it helps someone recognise a problem and understand a credible way to address it.",
        "4.2 The problem–solution structure\nA simple model of sales and storytelling is:",
